{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntemplate<typename T>\nvoid _print(const char *sdbg, T h) { cerr<<sdbg<<'='<<h<<endl; }\n\ntemplate<typename T, typename... Args>\nvoid _print(const char *sdbg, T h, Args... a) {\n  while(*sdbg!=',')cerr<<*sdbg++;\n  cerr<<'='<<h<<','; _print(sdbg+1, a...);\n}\n\ntemplate<typename T>\nostream& operator<<(ostream& os, const vector<T>& V) {\n  os << \"[\"; for (const auto& x : V) os << x << \",\"; return os << \"]\";\n}\n\ntemplate<typename L, typename R>\nostream& operator<<(ostream& os, const pair<L,R>& P) {\n  return os << \"(\" << P.first << \",\" << P.second << \")\";\n}\n\n#define trace(...) _print(#__VA_ARGS__, __VA_ARGS__)\n\nvector<long long> seq;\nlong long solve(long long n, long long idx) {\n\tlong long cnt = n / seq[idx];\n\tn %= seq[idx];\n  if(n == 0) {\n    return cnt * idx;\n  }\n  return cnt * idx + min(idx + solve(seq[idx] - n, idx - 1), solve(n, idx - 1));\n}\nint main() {\n  ios::sync_with_stdio(false); cin.tie(nullptr);\n  \n  long long test = 1, input;\n  long long cur = 0;\n  while(seq.size() < 17) {\n    seq.push_back(cur);\n    cur = cur * 10 + 1;\n  }\n  while(test--) {\n    cin >> input;\n    cout << solve(input, 16);\n  }\n  return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static List<Long> seq = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    private static void _print(String sdbg, Object... args) {\n        System.err.println(sdbg + \" = \" + Arrays.toString(args));\n    }\n\n    private static long solve(long n, long idx) {\n        long cnt = n / seq.get((int)idx);\n        n %= seq.get((int)idx);\n        if (n == 0) {\n            return cnt * idx;\n        }\n        return cnt * idx + Math.min(idx + solve(seq.get((int)idx) - n, idx - 1), solve(n, idx - 1));\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        \n        long cur = 0;\n        while (seq.size() < 17) {\n            seq.add(cur);\n            cur = cur * 10 + 1;\n        }\n        \n        long test = 1;\n        while (test-- > 0) {\n            long input = scanner.nextLong();\n            System.out.println(solve(input, 16));\n        }\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.75\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001292145170737058, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.23445157543756e-05, -3.2782016205601394e-05, -0.029803991317749023, -0.22600039839744568, -0.0003000047872774303, -8.344646857949556e-07, -4.1483970562694594e-05, -0.033646807074546814, -0.0041136653162539005, -0.25256237387657166, -1.6927575416048057e-05, -0.07208802551031113, -2.4914430468925275e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.3828182090946939e-05, -0.0023079682141542435, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.1086402082582936e-05, -0.5759772062301636, -1.9311717551317997e-05, -0.0067525296472013, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -0.12700973451137543, -0.5568908452987671, -6